  return '<div class="bar bpsx-share-price"><span class="q">'+esc(s.symbol)+' <b>$'+fmt(spot)+'</b></span><span class="note">'+esc(share.label)+' · ATM '+fmt(atm)+'</span><button class="mini" data-action="chain-atm" title="Reload the strike window around the share price">Show ATM strikes</button></div><p class="bpsx-selected-summary">'+summary+'</p>'+status+'<div class="bpsx-chain-table tblwrap"><table class="chain bpsx-chain"><thead><tr><th>Call bid / ask</th><th class="l"></th><th class="k">Strike</th><th>Put bid / ask</th><th class="l">+ BUY / − SELL</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+body+'</tbody></table></div><p class="note"><b>Feed ≠ tradability.</b> LIVE is IB market-data type 1, not proof of a regular-session, tight or executable market. Prices are raw IB Gateway bid/ask, per share (×100 per contract). Receipt times are not exchange-side timestamps. Wide/off-hours/illiquid quotes are never replaced by a model or invented midpoint. Recheck during regular option hours and compare the same conId/expiry in TWS. Same controls as Trade: <b>+ buys</b> the protective put; <b>− sells</b> the short put. Click a selected +/− again to deselect; click another strike to replace that leg. Calls are view-only in BPSX. '+ch.puts.length+' of '+(ch.listedPutCount||ch.puts.length)+' listed put strikes.</p>';
