 function guide(){return '<details id="bpsx-guide" class="bpsx-guide"><summary aria-label="BPSX construction quick guide">? · BPSX quick guide</summary><ol><li><b>Start at ATM and scan downward:</b> puts at/below the share quote only. The chain extends until observed deltas cover the target region plus protective strikes.</li><li><b>SELL the higher OTM put:</b> signed delta −0.09 to −0.15, target −0.10. <b>15% is a strong guideline, not a hard cutoff.</b> Buffer = (current share price − short strike) ÷ share price ×100, not distance from the listed ATM anchor. 1661 →1440 is <b>13.3%</b>; a 15% buffer needs a strike at/below 1411.85 (then use actual listed strikes). Delta is not a guaranteed probability of success.</li><li><b>When is 10–14% defensible?</b> The course explicitly allows a smaller buffer on less volatile names such as Pepsi / McDonald’s; about 10% may suffice in that context. It is not permission to use 12% on any stock. In the BABA example, about 12% was described as not ideal; Adam said he might not take it in reality and proceeded for demonstration, with trend strength as the conditional exception. NFLX had about 19%. Record evidence for lower volatility and tested support/trend if overriding 15%; otherwise skip or review another expiry/stock. Never move closer just to earn more premium. The 9–15 delta band (ceiling 15), wave down into support, 20–45 DTE, liquidity, no biotech/pharma or binary event, and earnings after expiry are not waived. The optional exact uptrend check is EMA20 >EMA40 AND SMA50 >SMA150.</li><li><b>BUY a lower put:</b> one or two actual listed strikes below, same expiry, 20–45 DTE (prefer about 26). This defines risk. Max loss must be ≤10× credit; each option’s bid/ask spread ≤ 0.4% of the share price (the course’s rule: $0.40 on a $100 stock, $0.80 on $200); adjustable or ignorable in the ticket.</li><li><b>Liquidity is separate from feed:</b> the course rule is a bid/ask width of at most 0.4% of the share price per option (so about $0.40 on a $100 stock); this app blocks new entry above it, adjustable with an Ignore switch. A $0.10 bid / $20 ask has a $19.90 width, not a plausible $10.05 fill. Selling that put and buying another with the same market gives $0.10 −$20 = <b>−$19.90/share natural credit</b> (a debit), so no qualifying credit spread. LIVE only names the IB feed type. Off-hours, absent market makers, stale side prices and illiquidity are possible causes, not proven from the label. Check regular option hours, OPRA permissions and the identical contract in TWS. A retained orange/blue selection is not a continuing recommendation; its current validity is shown above the table.</li><li><b>Position sizing:</b> reserve a strategy allocation, divide by ten for the open-premium cap, then by ten trades for the per-trade premium target. $20,000 →$2,000 total premium →$200 per trade; $0.50 credit ×100 = $50 per spread →4 spreads. Auto sizing recalculates on leg/credit/allocation/quote/account changes and is constrained by remaining premium, total defined risk, pending BPSX risk and account available funds. Whole quantities round DOWN here (conservative app policy, not a course hard rounding rule); never force one if it exceeds capacity/target. Editing quantity switches to a visible manual override; re-enable automatic sizing to resume. Ten diversified trades is a ceiling, not an obligation, and premium targets are not promised income.</li><li><b>Buttons:</b> − selects SELL; + selects BUY. Active buttons and orange/blue strike cells identify the current spread. Click the same active button again to deselect. Auto-selection uses these exact same states.</li><li><b>Dollar outcomes:</b> max profit = credit ×100×quantity; max loss = (strike width −credit) ×100×quantity. TP profit = 90% of credit; SL loss threshold = 3×credit, reached at a <b>4×credit closing debit</b>, not 3×.</li><li><b>Automatic PAPER exits:</b> armed only after the entry actually fills, based on its actual credit. TP closes at ≤0.1×credit debit; SL triggers a marketable paper buyback at ≥4×credit debit. An expiry-day safety close is attempted 5 minutes before the verified IB session end. These are sibling conditions for ONE closing combo, not two independent orders.</li><li><b>Limits:</b> keep this browser open, the correct paper account active, IB connected, and regular-session quotes fresh/live. No broker orders or off-browser protection. Gaps, liquidity, slippage and commissions can exceed the stop target. Course support/trend breakdown and revised earnings dates still require manual review; the course IV-only loss exception is discretionary and is NOT applied by the automatic hard stop.</li></ol></details>';}
 function payoff(){const s=selection,ch=s?.chain;if(!ch)return '';const short=ch.puts.find(r=>r.conid===s.short),long=ch.puts.find(r=>r.conid===s.long),e=C.economics(short,long,Number(ticket.credit),Number(ticket.qty)),dollar=v=>Number.isFinite(v)?'$'+v.toFixed(2):'—';return '<section class="bpsx-payoff" aria-label="Payoff preview"><dl class="bpsx-risk-grid"><div><dt>Maximum profit</dt><dd data-payoff="max-profit">'+dollar(e.maxProfit)+'</dd></div><div><dt>Maximum loss</dt><dd data-payoff="max-loss">'+dollar(e.maxLoss)+'</dd></div><div><dt>Expected TP profit · 90%</dt><dd data-payoff="tp-profit">'+dollar(e.takeProfitProfit)+'</dd></div><div><dt>SL loss threshold · 3× credit</dt><dd data-payoff="sl-loss">'+dollar(e.stopLossLoss)+'</dd></div></dl><p>TP buyback: '+fmt(e.takeProfitDebit)+' /share ('+dollar(e.takeProfitCost)+' total). SL trigger buyback: '+fmt(e.lossAlertDebit)+' /share ('+dollar(e.stopLossCost)+' total). Break-even '+fmt(e.breakeven)+' · risk/credit '+fmt(e.ratio)+'×.</p><p><b>Automatic paper TP/SL included.</b> Estimates use the entered credit; exits use the actual filled credit. All amounts before fees/slippage. SL is a trigger, not a guaranteed maximum loss. Active account/browser + fresh LIVE regular-session data required.</p></section>';}
